namespace Crateside.Core.Queue;

/// <summary>
/// Whether a queued video is likely to yield a YouTube Premium audio format when downloaded.
/// </summary>
public enum PremiumOutlook
{
    /// <summary>Nothing can be said — the item carries no description to judge by.</summary>
    Unknown,

    /// <summary>
    /// An auto-generated YouTube Music art track. Premium audio was provisioned for every
    /// one of these in the measured corpus.
    /// </summary>
    ArtTrack,

    /// <summary>
    /// An ordinary video upload. It may still carry premium audio, but it is the case where a
    /// better URL for the same song often exists.
    /// </summary>
    VideoUpload,
}

/// <summary>
/// Reads the premium outlook from what the YouTube Data API actually returns.
/// </summary>
/// <remarks>
/// <para>
/// <strong>The signal is the auto-generated marker in the video description.</strong> YouTube
/// ends the description of every auto-generated art track with "Auto-generated by YouTube."
/// and opens it with "Provided to YouTube by &lt;distributor&gt;".
/// </para>
/// <para>
/// <strong>Measured, not assumed.</strong> Against the 552-video corpus in
/// <c>V:\Repos\Yt-dlp_Formats</c>, which was resolved logged-out, signed-in-free and
/// signed-in-Premium:
/// </para>
/// <list type="bullet">
/// <item>The marker fires on exactly <strong>326</strong> videos, and that set is
/// <em>identical</em> to the set yt-dlp reports an <c>artist</c> for — the <c>artist</c>
/// field is StemForge's <c>IsMusicTrackEntity</c> test. So the API reproduces a signal that
/// was thought to need yt-dlp.</item>
/// <item>All <strong>326/326</strong> of those were provisioned premium audio. Zero false
/// positives.</item>
/// <item>Of the remaining 226, only 94 (42%) were premium — so the absence of the marker
/// predicts nothing, and must be reported as a caveat rather than as a failure.</item>
/// </list>
/// <para>
/// Two rejected alternatives, both measured on the same corpus: a channel title ending in
/// " - Topic" gets one false positive and is additionally misleading in the YouTube UI, which
/// displays art tracks under the official artist channel while the API still reports the
/// Topic channel. <c>categoryId == 10</c> (Music) fires on 496 with 88 false positives, and
/// <c>contentDetails.licensedContent</c> on 415 with 34 — neither is close.
/// </para>
/// </remarks>
public static class PremiumOutlookReader
{
    private const string AutoGeneratedMarker = "Auto-generated by YouTube";

    /// <summary>
    /// Judges a video from its description. Takes the description rather than making its own
    /// request: <c>playlistItems.list</c> already returns it, so the whole signal is free.
    /// </summary>
    public static PremiumOutlook FromDescription(string? description) =>
        description?.Trim() switch
        {
            not { Length: > 0 } => PremiumOutlook.Unknown,
            { } text when text.Contains(AutoGeneratedMarker, StringComparison.Ordinal) =>
                PremiumOutlook.ArtTrack,
            _ => PremiumOutlook.VideoUpload,
        };

    /// <summary>
    /// What to tell the user, or null when there is nothing worth saying. An art track gets no
    /// message: explaining a success is noise, and it keeps a visible flag meaningful.
    /// </summary>
    public static string? AdvisoryFor(PremiumOutlook outlook) =>
        outlook switch
        {
            PremiumOutlook.VideoUpload =>
                "A video upload rather than a YouTube Music track. It may still download at "
                    + "full quality — 42% of these did — but this is where a better URL for the "
                    + "same song usually exists. Worth checking for a song version before "
                    + "processing.",
            PremiumOutlook.Unknown =>
                "No description to judge by, so nothing can be said about the audio quality "
                    + "this will download at.",
            _ => null,
        };
}
